BT 1 0 0 1 0 127.0185 Tm .030998 Tw 14.91 TL /F2 10.5 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: A carrier is presumed at fault on a passenger death or injury, yet the presumption yields to proof of utmost diligence,) Tj T* 0 Tw (and a stranger attack still tests what diligence could have prevented.) Tj  T* .633148 Tw (The law presumes fault or negligence on death or injury under Art. 1756, so the carrier opens every case carrying the) Tj T* 0 Tw (burden of proving the extraordinary diligence of Arts. 1733 and 1755.) Tj  T* .646798 Tw (That diligence is the utmost care of very cautious persons with due regard for all the circumstances, and the carrier is) Tj T* 0 Tw .717279 Tw (no absolute insurer since an unforeseeable stranger act it could not have prevented with good-family vigilance breaks) Tj T* 0 Tw (liability under Art. 1759.) Tj  T* .98391 Tw (A fellow-passenger stabbing is judged the same way, since the carrier answers only where its employees could have) Tj T* 0 Tw (prevented or stopped the assault through the diligence the law demands.) Tj T* ET
