BT 1 0 0 1 0 112.1085 Tm .749581 Tw 14.91 TL /F2 10.5 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: The suitcase claimant proves turnover with loss at arrival while the laptop claimant must prove carrier fault, since) Tj T* 0 Tw (custody fixes the burden.) Tj  T* .653331 Tw (The tagged suitcase rode in carrier custody, so vanishing baggage raises the presumption of fault and the carrier must) Tj T* 0 Tw (prove extraordinary diligence or an Art. 1734 excuse.) Tj  T* .225439 Tw (The laptop stayed in passenger custody throughout, so no presumption runs and the passenger must show the snatching) Tj T* 0 Tw (came through employee fault or want of due precautions.) Tj  T* 1.53238 Tw (The first claim therefore succeeds on custody and loss alone unless rebutted, while the second needs specific fault) Tj T* 0 Tw (proved against the carrier.) Tj T* ET
