BT 1 0 0 1 0 171.822 Tm 1.920946 Tw 14.91 TL /F4 10.5 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (2019 Bar Q: LMN, Inc. operates a beach resort in a secluded island off the coast of Puerto Princesa City,) Tj T* 0 Tw .879235 Tw (Palawan. It operates three \(3\) motorized boats to ferry its guests from the city proper to the island resort and) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.393342 Tw (vice-versa. During one rainy morning, the guests were informed that the ferry services for that day were) Tj T* 0 Tw .701923 Tw (cancelled due to a storm forecast. In order to appease the apparent dismay of most of the guests who will miss) Tj T* 0 Tw .106656 Tw (their flight back to Manila, the boat captain of one of LMN, Inc.'s motorized boats decided to push through with) Tj T* 0 Tw .817948 Tw (its trip back to the city. Shortly after the boat sailed, the storm hit and the winds and waves became stronger,) Tj T* 0 Tw .014367 Tw (causing engine trouble to the boat. Unfortunately, the boat capsized and sank, resulting in the death of one of the) Tj T* 0 Tw .551831 Tw (passengers, Mr. X. This prompted Mr. X's heirs to file a complaint for damages against LMN, Inc., which they) Tj T* 0 Tw .250423 Tw (alleged to be a common carrier. In its defense, LMN, Inc. maintained that it is not a common carrier because its) Tj T* 0 Tw .661498 Tw (boats are not available to the general public but only ferry resort guests and employees. \(a\) May LMN, Inc. be) Tj T* 0 Tw .516351 Tw (considered a common carrier? Explain. \(3%\) \(b\) Assuming LMN, Inc. is a common carrier, may it be absolved) Tj T* 0 Tw (from liability on the ground of fortuitous event? Explain. \(2%\)) Tj T* ET
