BT 1 0 0 1 0 156.8385 Tm .391998 Tw 14.91 TL /F2 10.5 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: No to the blanket presumption, yet the diligence stays utmost and the fellow-passenger variant binds the line where) Tj T* 0 Tw (prevention was possible.) Tj  T* .719248 Tw (The presumption of Art. 1756 runs where death or injury attends carriage, and the carrier rebuts it only with proof of) Tj T* 0 Tw .188998 Tw (the extraordinary diligence of Arts. 1733 and 1755, so a stranger act is tested by preventability rather than by insurance) Tj T* 0 Tw (logic.) Tj  T* .251446 Tw (A rock from the roadside acquits where the crew could have done nothing with good-family care, since Art. 1763 frees) Tj T* 0 Tw (the carrier for stranger harm it could not have prevented or stopped.) Tj  T* .880423 Tw (A stabbing by a co-passenger binds where the crew could have prevented or stopped it with the same care, since the) Tj T* 0 Tw (article draws no line between strangers and fellow riders.) Tj  T* .419998 Tw (The heirs therefore face fair adjudication on prevention proof, with the rock case turning on the blind roadside and the) Tj T* 0 Tw (knife case turning on what the conductor saw and did.) Tj T* ET
