BT 1 0 0 1 0 112.182 Tm .643261 Tw 14.91 TL /F4 10.5 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (2017 Bar Q: Absolute Timber Co. \(ATC\) has been engaged in the logging business in Isabela. To secure one of) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.212165 Tw (its shipments of logs to be transported by Andok Shipping Co., ATC purchased a marine policy with an "all) Tj T* 0 Tw .444086 Tw (risks" provision. Because of a strong typhoon then hitting Northern Luzon, the vessel sank and the shipment of) Tj T* 0 Tw .998051 Tw (logs was totally lost. ATC filed its claim, but the insurer denied the claim on several grounds, namely: \(1\) the) Tj T* 0 Tw .790586 Tw (vessel had not been seaworthy; \(2\) the vessel's crew had lacked sufficient training; \(3\) the improper loading of) Tj T* 0 Tw .205624 Tw (the logs on only one side of the vessel had led to the tilting of the ship to that side during the stormy voyage; and) Tj T* 0 Tw .235198 Tw (\(4\) the extremely bad weather had been a fortuitous event. ATC now seeks your legal advice to know if its claim) Tj T* 0 Tw (was sustainable. What is your advice? Explain your answer. \(3%\)) Tj T* ET
