BT 1 0 0 1 0 156.8385 Tm .558998 Tw 14.91 TL /F2 10.5 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: I advise ATC that its claim is sustainable and that the four grounds for denial all fail against the carrier negligence) Tj T* 0 Tw (shown.) Tj  T* 1.918873 Tw (A common carrier must observe extraordinary diligence and a typhoon that regularly visits Northern Luzon is an) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.806298 Tw (ordinary vicissitude of the voyage rather than a fortuitous event once unseaworthiness, an untrained crew, and) Tj T* 0 Tw (one-sided loading concurred to sink the vessel.) Tj  T* .603748 Tw (The unseaworthy condition at sailing, the lack of crew training, and the improper stowage point to concurrent fault of) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.492103 Tw (the shipowner, so the defense of force majeure collapses and the limited liability rule of no vessel and no liability) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.364998 Tw (cannot shelter the owner under the doctrine of ) Tj /F3 10.5 Tf (Phil-Am General Insurance Co., Inc. v. Court of Appeals) Tj /F2 10.5 Tf ( \(G.R. No.) Tj T* 0 Tw (116940, 1997\).) Tj  T* 2.23588 Tw (ATC therefore recovers on the all-risks policy and the insurer as subrogee takes the same action against Andok) Tj T* 0 Tw (Shipping, because the proximate cause of the total loss was carrier fault and not the weather alone.) Tj T* ET
