BT 1 0 0 1 0 112.1085 Tm .343581 Tw 14.91 TL /F2 10.5 Tf .066667 .066667 .066667 rg (A: The captain must present himself to the maritime authority within twenty-four hours and file a sworn declaration of) Tj T* 0 Tw (the vessel name, registry, port of departure, cargo, and cause of arrival.) Tj  T* .703498 Tw (Article 612 makes this protest an inherent duty of the captain whenever he makes a port in distress, and the authority) Tj T* 0 Tw (vises the declaration when found acceptable.) Tj  T* .695209 Tw (The vised certificate proving arrival in distress and its reasons is the paper that proves compliance, and it anchors the) Tj T* 0 Tw (later ruling on whether the arrival was proper or improper.) Tj  T* .586893 Tw (Without that timely protest the shipowner loses the evidentiary root of a proper arrival and stays exposed to the cargo) Tj T* 0 Tw (claims the voyage break caused.) Tj T* ET
